I'm sorry, your logic eludes me.  While being held, fighters can still use
two handed weapons with no penalty, or a single-hander and a shield, again
with no penalty.  Being held doesn't seem to affect your arms at all, and
thus shouldn't affect spells.  Slightly more formally:

Given (1): shields don't hamper single-handed weapon use.
Given (2): shields prevent two-handed weapon use.
Given (3): shields hamper magic.
Deduction (a, from 1, 2, and 3): magic requires the use of both arms, though
not to the same extent as two-handed weapons.
Given (4): being held doesn't affect any combat.
Given (5): combat requires one or both arms, and sometimes the legs
(kicking).
Deduction (b, from 4 and 5): being held doesn't affect the arms (or legs).
Deduction (c, from a and b): being held doesn't affect spell casting (QED).

Of course, this leaves open the question of why spell-casting doens't
require a dexterity check, but since that wasn't in your post, I'll leave it
for another discussion...

